# Lives in main/ (ESP-IDF reads Kconfig.projbuild from components only, not the project root).
menu "ELLM chat"
    config CHAT_DISPLAY
        bool "Use the AMOLED"
        default y
        help
            Draw on the AMOLED (the chat screen, or the tok/s number: CHAT_SCREEN_TEXT). Switch
            off only to measure the screen's cost (Plan 4 Tasks 5 and 14): with n the panel is
            never initialized.
    config CHAT_SCREEN_TEXT
        bool "Chat screen (reply text, state, context bar, tok/s)"
        default y
        depends on CHAT_DISPLAY
        help
            The chat screen (docs/stages/screen-design.md): thinking/writing/idle, the context
            fill, the user line and the streaming reply (last 9 rows, Latin-1), the live tok/s.
            n: only the live tok/s number, 0 when idle (the Task 5 screen; the fallback if the
            chat screen ever costs more than 3 % of tok/s).
    config CHAT_PREFETCH
        bool "DCache autoload (prefetch) over the PSRAM arena"
        default y
        help
            Enable the DCache autoload over the PSRAM arena (core, KV, logits), as firmware/app
            does: ~5 % faster decode (measured on the chat: 3.61 -> 3.79 tok/s, +4.9 %, Plan 4
            Task 5; Plan 3: 4-5 % per token). The +13 % in the spec is the S0 matvec kernel
            alone; the flash-bound head and the attention gain less. With n it stays off
            (fallback if prefetch misbehaves: ship it off and record the cost). The banner
            reports prefetch=on|off.
    config CHAT_DEBUG_STACK
        bool "Stack high-water marks in the stats line (debug)"
        default n
        help
            Append ", stack_free=<B> worker_stack_free=<B>" (lifetime minimum free stack of the
            main task and the core-1 worker) inside the stats line brackets. Debug builds only:
            the normal protocol has no such field.
endmenu
